<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Commandery</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as commanderies</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A commandery was a large administrative unit of imperial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, divided into counties and governed by officials appointed by the central government. The system originated under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> and was extended by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a>. Commanderies allowed the Han court to administer its territories directly, alongside semi-autonomous kingdoms.</p></div>
